      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pulmonary embolism is one of the differential diagnoses of \"acute chest\" syndromes. We report a clinical case of contained rupture of ascending aortic aneurysm with pulmonary arteries compression, which was presented as pulmonary embolism, and we well review the literature data of this diagnostic trap."},
